DESCRIPTION:Friends of Lower Haw is having an invasive plant removal workda
 y with NC State Parks biologists on September 9th from 9:30 am until 3:00 
 pm\, or whenever you need to leave. Meeting location is the parking lot at
  4551 US Hwy 15-501 N\, Pittsboro. Meet in the parking lot at 9:30 am and 
 stay however long you want to help. We will be working in the Pegg Tract a
 rea of the Lower Haw River State Natural Area\, located upstream of the By
 num Dam by US Hwy 15-501. Invasive plant workdays involve identifying and 
 removing non-native plants using clippers\, pruners\, saws\, and other non
 -motorized hand tools. Learn about invasive plants and removal techniques.
  Hand tools will be available\, or volunteers can bring their own loppers 
 or hand pruners.  Bring your own work gloves\, insect repellent\, and drin
 king water. Long pants\, long sleeve shirt\, and closed toe shoes are reco
 mmended. There are no restroom facilities at this location. Youth voluntee
 rs under age 18 are welcome to participate with signed parental consent fo
 rm.\n\nBased on new regulations\, volunteers who may be interested in appl
 ying herbicide are now required to watch the new NCDA required training vi
 deo (34 minutes) for non-licensed pesticide applicators before attending t
 he workday.  You can still volunteer if you are not interested in applying
  herbicide and will not need to watch the training video.
GEO:35.771669;-79.142253
LOCATION:Lower Haw River State Natural Area 
SUMMARY:Whack Attack Invasive Plant Removal Workday
