DTSTAMP:20260905T041912Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53879011750936
DTSTART:20260910T223000Z
DTEND:20260911T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Stone Center’s Diaspora Festival of Black & Independent F
 ilm returns for another powerful celebration of cinema\, storytelling\, an
 d voices from across the African diaspora.\n\n \n\nSince 2004\, the festiv
 al has brought audiences together for compelling films\, engaging conversa
 tions\, and thought-provoking dialogue with filmmakers\, scholars\, and ou
 r community.\n\n \n\n✨ Opening Night\n📅 Thursday\, Sept. 10\n⏰ 6:30
  p.m.\n📍 Sonja Haynes Stone Center\n🎥 Three must-see films\n💫 Fre
 e & open to all\n\n \n\nCome experience an unforgettable evening of film a
 nd conversation as we kick off this year’s festival. We can’t wait to 
 see you there!\n\n \n\nRSVP: https://go.unc.edu/filmfest2026
GEO:35.907852;-79.050272
LOCATION:The Sonja Haynes Stone Center for Research in Black Culture and Hi
 story\, Hitchcock Room
