X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/national-day-of-service-clean-up-day-with-riverlink-and-buncombe-250"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041836Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53693228320319
DTSTART:20260911T140000Z
DTEND:20260911T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join RiverLink for a "National Day of Service" clean-up day\, h
 eld in partnership with America 250 NC Buncombe County. Together\, we will
  promote the environmental and economic vitality of the French Broad River
  and its watershed as a place to live\, learn\, work\, and play.\n\nAbout 
 the Clean Up:\n\nKaren Cragnolin Park (KCP) was purchased as a long-standi
 ng auto-crushing junkyard in 2006. For almost two decades\, RiverLink inve
 sted in the property by removing concrete\, healing the polluted soil\, an
 d managing invasive plants. In 2023 we connected the paved greenway path t
 o the parks on each side and opened these five acres as a public park---on
 e that showcases its context in nature and cultural history\, tells its st
 ory of remediation\, and honors RiverLink’s founder\, Karen Cragnolin. D
 esigned with flood resilience in mind\, KCP performed beautifully during H
 urricane Helene despite being under some 20 feet of moving water. We conti
 nue to invest in the park’s resilience by caring for the native pollinat
 or meadow in partnership with Patchwork Meadows\, enhancing our riparian a
 rea\, and creating an aesthetically pleasing\, educational\, climate resil
 ient public park for the community to enjoy.  \n\nFor this event\, we will
  continue this work by managing the non-native invasive plant species in t
 he meadow and supporting newly planted trees and shrubs along the river ba
 nk. Expect light to moderate gardening work (weeding\, mulching\, watering
 ).\n\nHow to be Prepared: RiverLink will provide all necessary tools and e
 quipment. Closed-toed shoes are required and pants are recommended. We als
 o recommend everyone bring a water bottle and gardening gloves if you have
  them\, but gloves will be provided if needed.\n\nFollow the link below to
  sign up for the clean up! https://riverlink.salsalabs.org/dayofservice/in
 dex.html\n\nWe look forward to seeing you there!
GEO:35.566366;-82.572511
LOCATION:Karen Cragnolin Park
SUMMARY:National Day of Service Clean Up Day with RiverLink and Buncombe 25
 0
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/national-day-of-service-clea
 n-up-day-with-riverlink-and-buncombe-250
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Statewide Clean Up
END:VEVENT
