DESCRIPTION:This event is FREE to the public!<br><br>Enjoy free music and 
 performance art\, visit our community partner tables\, and take home new E
 no River Association merchandise.<br><br><strong><b>Live Performances</b><
 /strong><br><a href="https://www.paperhandpuppet.org/" target="_blank"><st
 rong><b><em><i>Paperhand Puppet Intervention</i></em></b></strong></a> 
 – Beloved local artists bringing imaginative puppetry and visual storyte
 lling to the celebration.<br><strong><b><em><i><a href="https://www.facebo
 ok.com/FivePointsRounders/" target="_blank">Five Points Rounders</a> with
  Rowdy Square Dance (Caller Simone Fine)</i></em></b></strong> – An ene
 rgetic old-time string band accompanied by an interactive community square
  dance.<br><a href="https://www.instagram.com/durhamlaborchoir?utm_source=
 ig_web_button_share_sheet&amp\;igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==" target="_blank"><em>
 <i><strong><b>Durham Labor Choir </b></strong></i></em></a>– A communit
 y choir performing labor and movement songs that celebrate worker power th
 rough traditional favorites and contemporary arrangements.<br><a href="htt
 ps://duodantan.com/" target="_blank"><strong><b><em><i>Duo d’Antan</i></
 em></b></strong></a> – A duo performing an eclectic blend of Parisian m
 usette\, Brazilian choro\, swing\, Irish folk\, and traditional café musi
 c.<br><br><strong><b>Interactive Activities</b></strong><br><a href="https
 ://www.scrapexchange.org/" target="_blank"><strong><b><em><i>The Scrap Exc
 hange</i></em></b></strong></a> – Reuse-focused crafting activities usi
 ng reclaimed materials.<br><strong><b><em><i>Eno River Community Mural</i>
 </em></b></strong> – A live mural painting with opportunities for commu
 nity members to contribute to the artwork.<br><strong><b><em><i><a href="h
 ttps://shop.enofest.org/" target="_blank">ERA Merchandise Station</a> (
 “Little Big Top”)</i></em></b></strong> – Commemorative merchandise
  celebrating the Association’s 60th anniversary.<br><a href="https://www
 .enoriver.org/"><strong><b><em><i>ERA Information Booth</i></em></b></stro
 ng></a> – Learn about conservation initiatives\, volunteer opportunitie
 s\, and ways to support the Eno River Association.<br><br>Whether you’ve
  been part of our community for decades or are just getting to know the En
 o\, the plaza celebration is <strong><b>free and open to everyone.</b></s
 trong>
