SUMMARY:Nasher Teen Council (NTC) - Applications Open!
DESCRIPTION:The Nasher Teen Council is currently accepting applications for the 2026 – 2027 school year! \nThe Nasher Teen Council (NTC) is a free after-school program for Durham County high school students. The NTC meets every Thursday evening throughout the school year (October – April) from 5:30 – 7:30 PM\, with the exception of breaks and holidays. Snacks\, dinner\, and parking are provided at all meetings. \nDuring the 2026 – 2027 school year\, the NTC will curate an exhibition focused on the environment\, climate\, and sustainability! Through this process\, students will gain behind-the-scenes experience in exhibition-making within art museums and engage in critical conversations about environmental justice. \nPrior arts and museum experience are not required. All students with an interest in art\, research and writing\, environmental sciences\, and community building are encouraged to apply! \nApplications are due September 13\, 2026 by 11:59 PM.
URL:https://resilientdurhamnc.org/event/nasher-teen-council-ntc-applications-open/
END:VEVENT
