X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041912Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53578379905780
DTSTART:20260915T180000Z
DTEND:20260915T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:ArcGIS Pro is one of the most widely used GIS software platform
 s\, with a range of applications that include business analytics\, natural
  and health sciences\, transportation\, and more. Its suite of tools offer
 s capabilities for analytics and data science\, automation\, data manageme
 nt and editing\, image analysis\, and artificial intelligence.\n\nThis han
 ds-on course for beginners will provide an overview of ArcGIS Pro\, includ
 ing its layout and capabilities. Topics covered will include importing geo
 graphic data\, styling and symbolizing data\, querying and selecting data\
 , making basic maps\, and more!\n\n \n\nNote: While everyone is welcome to
  join this workshop\, we can only facilitate access to ArcGIS Pro for UNC-
 Chapel Hill affiliates.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is offered by the University
  Library and will be led by librarian Philip McDaniel. \n\n \n\nThis works
 hop is being offered remotely via Zoom. Register here: https://calendar.li
 b.unc.edu/event/17229080
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:ArcGIS Pro for Beginners
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/arcgis-pro-for-beginners-4534
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
