BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_newhopeaudubon
SUMMARY:NHBA Bird Outing
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260916T073000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260916T103000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041904Z
UID:5nagi8pmoda376ie25chd26kem@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260916T073000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260826T014237Z
DESCRIPTION:Contact David Anderson at <a href="mailto:d47anders@gmail.com
 " target="_blank"><u><u>d47anders@gmail.com</u></u></a> with questions. 
 The location will be Old Bynum Bridge\, Bynum Rd\, Pittsboro\, NC. The sit
 e is mostly flat and paved. Take 501 south from Chapel Hill (or north out 
 of Pittsboro).<br>  <br>If travelling south: As you approach the Haw Rive
 r\, shortly after Allen and Son Bar-B-Que\, and just before the bridge ove
 r the Haw River\, you will turn left onto Durham-Eubanks Road.<br><br> If
  travelling north from Pittsboro: Durham Eubanks Road is the first right a
 fter the Haw Bridge.<br>  <br>Take Durham Eubanks until it tees out on By
 num Road. Turn right\, toward the river\, and go to the end of the road. T
 here is a parking lot on the left (The only parking is on the north side o
 f the Haw River – there is no parking on the south side).  <br><br>This
  outing is sponsored by the New Hope Bird Alliance (formerly New Hope Audu
 bon).<br><br>Outings usually last 2-3 hours. No reservations or sign-up ne
 eded. If there is a large turnout for any particular outing\, we may split
  into two groups. We do recommend carpooling for families or friend pods\;
  while we love pets\, there is a ‘no-pet’ policy for bird outings. New
  birders and birders of all skill levels are welcome. <br><br>Please wear
  long pants\, socks\, and sturdy shoes (ticks and chiggers may be present)
 . Sun and bug protection are also recommended. Bring snacks and water if y
 ou like. Heavy rain will result in cancellation.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260826T014237Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:New Hope Bird Alliance
END:VEVENT
