X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Data Science Nc": "https://www.meetup.com/data-science-nc/events/315068280/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_data_science_nc
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Data Science Raleigh
UID:event_315068280@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041821Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260916T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260916T150000
SUMMARY:Seeing Is Believing: Observability as the Backbone of Trustworthy 
 AI
DESCRIPTION:Data Science Raleigh\nIt’s one thing for AI to work—it’s
  another to understand how and why it’s working. As AI systems move into
  production and touch more critical workflows\, observability becomes non-
 negotiable. Performance metrics alone aren’t enough\; leaders need insig
 ht into model behavior\, input drift\, and downstream impacts to maintain 
 trust and control.\n\nThis webinar explores the principles and practices o
 f AI observability: what to monitor\, how to measure it\, and how to respo
 nd. We’ll break down what meaningful observability looks like across the
  AI lifecycle—and why it’s foundational for governance\, risk mitigati
 on\, and long-term success.\n\n**What You'll Learn:**\n\n1️⃣ **Beyond 
 Accuracy:** What to track when accuracy isn’t the only—or best—indic
 ator of AI health.\n\n2️⃣ **Behavioral Monitoring:** Techniques to det
 ect drift\, distributional shift\, and changes in model reasoning over tim
 e.\n\n3️⃣**Downstream Risk Visibility:** How to trace model outputs th
 rough business processes to assess and manage their real-world impact.\n\n
 4️⃣**Enabling Governance:** How observability supports audits\, incide
 nt response\, and cross-functional accountability.\n\n**[Register here](ht
 tps://hubs.ly/Q04jJdVJ0)**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/data-science-nc/events/315068280/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260602T122207Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260602T122207Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
