SUMMARY:Native Plant Swap
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T120000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041904Z
UID:00l2q715tvntl04088enm75rrj@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T100000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260819T162524Z
DESCRIPTION:<br>Join New Hope Audubon Society’s Bird-Friendly Habitat te
 am at Blackwood Farm Park in Chapel Hill  for a free native plant swap! 
 All are welcome\, if you have plants to swap or not.<br><br>Bring transpla
 nted native plants in old nursery pots or bags that you are willing to par
 t with. Folks who bring plants to “swap” will have an opportunity to p
 ick plants one at a time from the available selection. Any extra plants wi
 ll be free to take for anyone who does not have plants to donate. We will 
 do our best to distribute plants evenly across attendees.<br><br>Please RS
 VP (but not required) by sending an email to <a target="_blank" href="mai
 lto:newhopebird@gmail.com"><u>newhopebird@gmail.com</u></a> and let us kn
 ow what you might bring. If you'd like to volunteer to help with the event
 \, please let us know!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T162656Z
LOCATION:Blackwood Farm Park\, Chapel Hill
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:New Hope Bird Alliance
END:VEVENT
