BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/hanging-rock-state-park/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260919T193000
DTSTAMP:20260812T143713Z
CREATED:20260812T143712Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260812T143713Z
UID:10001730-1789824600-1789846200@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Hanging Rock State Park – From Reservoir to Ridgeline (Danbury)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF Triad Wild Chapter and log your last summer hike at Hanging Rock State Park (and hopefully spot some early signs of autumn during the last weekend of summer!) \nThis 3-mile hike shows off some of the lesser-hiked parts of one of North Carolina’s oldest state parks. With a 429-foot elevation change\, hikers are encouraged to consider the climb and descent. The hike will be worth it; ascending among the boulders\, hikers are rewarded with views overlooking Winston-Salem\, Greensboro\, and even High Point visible on a clear day! \nAs hawk and raptor migration couples with fall bird migrations\, bird activity will be near its peak. Birders may get to catch a last glance of summertime birds like the summer tanager\, black-and-white warbler\, and great-crested flycatcher while hawks and falcons pass overhead! Leaves will begin showing signs of fall colors to come\, with the green peaks and valleys of summer still visible before the cold season kicks off. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/hanging-rock-state-park/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/septemberbirding.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/choosing-sides-the-catawba-nation-the-fight-for-independence"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041836Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53312428100030
DTSTART:20260919T140000Z
DTEND:20260919T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the Catawba Cultural Center\, Kings Mountai
 n Historical Museum is excited to present\, "Choosing Sides: The Catawba N
 ation & the Fight for Independence." This exhibit explores the critical ro
 le of the Catawba Nation\, also known as Yį Iswąre or “People of the R
 iver\,” in the American Revolutionary War\, particularly in the backcoun
 try regions of Tryon and Lincoln Counties. As skilled warriors\, guides\, 
 and allies of the Patriot cause\, the Catawba people defended their homela
 nd\, protected settler communities\, and contributed to pivotal battles. D
 espite the hardships of disease\, displacement\, and warfare\, the Catawba
  demonstrated extraordinary resilience. Their story is one of courage\, al
 liance\, and survival\, woven into the struggle for independence in the So
 uthern Campaign of the Revolution.\n\nThe exhibit will run from June 30\, 
 2026 until October 24\, 2026. Admission is Free!
GEO:35.239004;-81.342181
LOCATION:Kings Mountain Historical Museum
SUMMARY:Choosing Sides: The Catawba Nation & The Fight for Independence
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/choosing-sides-the-catawba-n
 ation-the-fight-for-independence
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
