BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/iah-fellows-forum-art-is-everything"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041913Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53701638569831
DTSTART:20260924T161000Z
DTEND:20260924T171000Z
DESCRIPTION:On Sept. 24\, English and comparative literature professor Step
 hanie Elizondo Griest (FFP ’15\, ’23) will give a Fellows Forum presen
 tation titled\, “Art is Everything.”\n\nIs art enough?\n\n\nAll artist
 s struggle. But women are especially pushed to give up their creative ambi
 tions\, from societal disapproval against “selfishness” to the pressur
 e (or desire) for children and economic stability. After spending much of 
 her twenties and thirties wondering if prioritizing her writing over every
 thing else was leading her to fulfillment or regret\, Stephanie Elizondo G
 riest turned to other women for their perspectives on that haunting questi
 on: is art enough? Her 2025 book Art Above Everything documents her travel
 s to 10 nations—from Cuba to Iceland\; Rwanda to Qatar—where she inter
 views legendary painters\, poets\, actors\, dancers\, and musicians who ta
 lk intimately about their art\, both what it gifts them and what it costs 
 them. Join us for a multi-media presentation and discussion about the real
 ities of placing art at the core of your existence.\n\nIntroductions will 
 begin at 12:10. The presentation will be from 12:15 – 12:45 p.m.\, with 
 a Q&A session to follow. Refreshments will be served.\n\nRSVP for the Fell
 ows Forum on Jotform.\n\n \n\nSee all events in the IAH Fellows Forum seri
 es.
GEO:35.913407;-79.052875
LOCATION:Hyde Hall\, University Room
SUMMARY:IAH Fellows Forum: Art is Everything
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/iah-fellows-forum-art-is-every
 thing
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/beginr-3408"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041913Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53578318785278
DTSTART:20260924T163000Z
DTEND:20260924T174500Z
DESCRIPTION:Learning R on your own? Want some help along the way? beginR is
  a series of virtual meetings organized by the University Libraries and th
 e Odum Institute that provides support to students\, faculty and staff who
  are learning the R programming language. The first week\, the instructors
  will introduce attendees to R\, help them install the software\, and shar
 e the materials that will be covered in subsequent meetings. In the follow
 ing weeks\, beginR attendees will learn R by following the lessons on the 
 R Open Labs website at their own pace. Each week\, staff will be available
  via Zoom to answer questions\, solve problems and provide the solutions t
 o exercises.\n\n \n\nbeginR is a collaboration between the University Libr
 ary and the Odum Institute. The workshops will be led by librarians Lorin 
 Bruckner and Matt Jansen\, and Nuvan Rathnayaka from the Odum Institute. \
 n\n \n\nThis workshop is being offered remotely via Zoom only. Register he
 re: https://calendar.lib.unc.edu/event/17229647
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:beginR
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/beginr-3408
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-in-research-series-ai-for-programming-9388"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041913Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52259562235016
DTSTART:20260924T170000Z
DTEND:20260924T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:AI in Research: Driving Innovation Forward\n\nDiscover how arti
 ficial intelligence can streamline workflows\, uncover hidden patterns\, a
 nd empower breakthroughs in your field. Learn practical applications of AI
  through Odum Institute AIR series that can revolutionize your research pr
 ocess.\n\nAI\, for example ChatGPT\, may be used to construct code for sof
 tware packages and programming languages commonly used by social scientist
 s. Examples include SAS\, Stata and R. The quality of responses has varied
  to this point and may continue to at the time of the class. Examples will
  be given.\n\nYou must have a UNC Chapel Hill Onyen to register and attend
  this course. No registration fees required but you must register to secur
 e your spot and receive the Zoom link.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:AI in Research Series – AI for Programming
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-in-research-series-ai-for-p
 rogramming-9388
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/no-water-no-beer-asheville/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260924T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260924T200000
DTSTAMP:20260817T163541Z
CREATED:20260730T191428Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260817T163541Z
UID:10001703-1790269200-1790280000@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:No Water No Beer (Asheville)
DESCRIPTION:No water\, no beer. It really is that simple. Every pint poured in North Carolina starts with clean\, reliable water\, and the people who make that happen are the water professionals in this room. Join NC One Water at Burial Brewing at Forestry Camp for an evening of craft beer\, good food\, and better conversation. Your ticket includes one drink token and one food token\, and ReWild AVL will be on site\, a chapter of the North Carolina Wildlife Federation working to restore habitat and protect western North Carolina waterways. Bring a colleague\, bring a friend\, and raise a glass to the water that makes it all possible. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/no-water-no-beer-asheville/
CATEGORIES:Featured
END:VEVENT
