DESCRIPTION:SAVE THE DATE! Join us for our annual Educator Open House and S
 ciREN Triangle Networking Event on Thursday\, September 24\, 2026 from 6:0
 0–8:30pm. This special information exchange night is just for educators 
 and will feature local scientists\, Museum educators and partner organizat
 ions showcasing their FREE lesson plans and resources in a relaxed environ
 ment. Learn about new programs and field trips\, outreach and virtual prog
 rams\, and professional development opportunities.\n\nThrough a partnershi
 p with SciREN (Scientific Research and Education Network)\, meet local sci
 entists ready to distribute curriculum-correlated lessons based on their c
 urrent research! This is an excellent way to rejuvenate teaching methods\,
  integrate relevant and real science into student learning\, and reach out
  into the community.\n\nWhat to Expect\n\nFree: dinner!!Free: beverages co
 urtesy of New Belgium BrewingFree: curriculum-correlated K–12 lesson pla
 ns (including digital access)Opportunities to talk 1:1 with scientistsInfo
 rmation about program offerings from the Museum and other partner organiza
 tionsTake a tour of the Museum’s galleries and exhibits.Learn about upco
 ming professional development opportunities.Event Details\n\nFREE\, but re
 gistration is required.\n\nIf you are an EDUCATOR\, register here!\n\nIf y
 ou are a SCIENTIST or EXHIBITOR\, register here!\n\nLocation: NC Museum of
  Natural Sciences\, Nature Exploration Center — Directions and Parking
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SUMMARY:SciREN and Educator Open House
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/sciren-and-educator-open-hou
 se
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
