X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncbg": "https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/fall-plant-sale/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncbg
X-SOURCE:NC Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260926T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260926T130000
DTSTAMP:20260820T141723Z
CREATED:20260818T141201Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260820T141723Z
UID:10000866-1790413200-1790427600@ncbg.unc.edu
SUMMARY:Fall Plant Sale
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, September 26\n9 a.m. – 1 p.m.\nFree and open to all \nJoin us for our annual Fall Plant Sale to find new southeastern native plants for your garden! \nWe grow the southeastern native wildflowers\, grasses\, shrubs\, trees\, vines\, ferns\, and carnivorous plants for sale right here in our nursery. Proceeds support our research in plant conservation and propagation. \nWe’ll update this description with a list of plant species when that’s available! \nMEMBERS’ SALE \nNCBG Foundation Members enjoy a 10% discount on plants and the opportunity to sign up for an early access sale on Friday\, September 25. \nWHY NATIVE PLANTS? \nGardening with native plants restores lost connections between plants and wildlife. And since they’re adapted to the soils\, climates\, diseases\, and predators of our region\, native plants may require fewer pesticides and expensive management practices and be more likely to thrive in a garden. Learn more on our Resources for Gardeners page > \nWHY FALL? \nFall is the best time to plant North Carolina’s wonderful native perennials\, shrubs\, trees\, ferns\, and grasses: it gives plant times to establish their root systems prior to the growing season.
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/fall-plant-sale/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Special Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncbg.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/963/2019/07/DSC_0415.jpg
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=North Carolina Botanical Garden 100 Old Mason Farm Road Chapel Hill NC 27517 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=100 Old Mason Farm Road:geo:-79.031939,35.901081
END:VEVENT
