DTSTAMP:20260905T041836Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53674611958477
DTSTART:20260926T150000Z
DTEND:20260926T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Calling all young explorers! On National Public Lands Day (9/26
 ) and as part of Take A Child Outside Week (Sept 24-30)\, meet a park rang
 er at The Iron Ore Belt Access for a leisurely  hike that mixes science\, 
 history\, and conservation. Paticipants will be issued a junior ranger boo
 klet at the trailhead and guidance for working through the activities with
  the goal of earning the park's junior ranger patch by the end of our adve
 nture. Plan for a 1.5-2.0 mile\, relatively-flat hike over natural surface
  trails\, mostly shaded but with potential for some open\, sunny areas. No
  two hikes are ever alike... What will you discover on our walk through th
 e woods?\n\nPlease wear close-toed shoes\, a hat or umbrella for sun prote
 ction if you like\, and bring bottled water plus whatever you need to be c
 omfortable for a two-hour nature walk. The Junior Ranger Program is geared
  towards children ages 5-12 years old\; adult guardians must accompany chi
 ldren. Registration not required but encouraged to help with planning.
GEO:36.23742;-79.785591
LOCATION:Haw River State Park - Iron Ore Belt Access 
SUMMARY:Junior Ranger Discovery Hike
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/junior-ranger-discovery-hike
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Nature & Wildlife Programs
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Youth & Family Activities
END:VEVENT
