DTEND:20260926T181500Z
DESCRIPTION:To learn a fuller story of the people who worked in tobacco\, j
 oin Duke Homestead staff on site for a special program\, “Field & Factor
 y: A Look at Tobacco’s Laborers.” These walks will highlight the contr
 ibutions that each group of people working in tobacco made to North Caroli
 na’s culture and powerful economy in the late 19th and early 20th centur
 ies\, while addressing the inequalities in tobacco’s labor forces.\n\nWe
  will depart from the visitor’s center lobby at 11:15am and 2:15pm on Sa
 turday\, September 5th\, 12th\, 19th\, and 26th. Admission is free.
GEO:36.035768;-78.920968
LOCATION:Duke Homestead
SUMMARY:"Field & Factory: A Look at Tobacco’s Laborers" at Duke Homestead
