UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53816697740825
DTSTART:20260928T123000Z
DTEND:20260928T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Attention all hikers/birders! Come out and help count migrating
  hawks at Hanging Rock State Park!\n\nParticipants will meet in front of t
 he Visitor Center at 8:30 am for introductions. Afterward\, we will carpoo
 l to the campground to access the Moore’s Wall Loop Trail leading to the
  fire tower.\n\nThe hike to the tower is a total of 2 miles round trip and
  is strenuous\, so please bring food and water. Join us to learn how to id
 entify raptors in flight and help monitor the annual hawk migration. All d
 ata collected will be submitted to the Hawk Migration Association of North
  America’s raptor migration database.\n\nBinoculars and a spotting scope
  will be available for participants to use. To sign up\, please email me a
 t jonathan.buie@ncparks.gov. The program will be limited to 10 participant
 s.
GEO:36.395044;-80.266541
LOCATION:Hanging Rock State Park\, Visitor Center
SUMMARY:Hawk Watch
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/hawk-watch-9667
