DTSTART:20261003T140000Z
DTEND:20261003T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Interprofessional Design-a-thon at the Inpatient Rehabilita
 tion Center brings together student teams to apply human-centered design t
 hinking to address patient needs. Student teams collaborate on a solution 
 and present their idea to a panel of faculty and health professionals\, wh
 o then select a winning team. This is an approved IPEP Distinguished Schol
 ars Immersion hosted by the Office of Interprofessional Education and Prac
 tice.\n\n \n\nFall 2026 Design-a-thon:\n\nSaturday\, October 3 from 10 a.m
 . to 3 p.m.\n\nSaturday\, October 10 from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m.\n\n \n\nDesign
 -a-thon Eligibility:\n\nComplete basic BEAM Makerspace training.Be availab
 le all 5 hours on each Saturday (10 hours total) and complete independent 
 work (research\, faculty consultation\, etc.) in the week between.Designed
  for medical\, nursing\, biomedical engineering\, physical therapy\, clini
 cal rehabilitation and mental health counseling\, occupational therapy\, s
 peech therapy and pharmacy students. Other students can apply\, and their 
 participation will be considered as space allows.​Applications are revie
 wed as received and the deadline to apply is September 1\, 2026. Questions
 ? Email unc_ipe@unc.edu.
GEO:36.037842;-79.090807
LOCATION:UNC Hospitals Hillsborough Campus
SUMMARY:Interprofessional Design-a-thon
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/interprofessional-design-a-tho
 n
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/choosing-sides-the-catawba-nation-the-fight-for-independence"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041837Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53312428110280
DTSTART:20261003T140000Z
DTEND:20261003T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the Catawba Cultural Center\, Kings Mountai
 n Historical Museum is excited to present\, "Choosing Sides: The Catawba N
 ation & the Fight for Independence." This exhibit explores the critical ro
 le of the Catawba Nation\, also known as Yį Iswąre or “People of the R
 iver\,” in the American Revolutionary War\, particularly in the backcoun
 try regions of Tryon and Lincoln Counties. As skilled warriors\, guides\, 
 and allies of the Patriot cause\, the Catawba people defended their homela
 nd\, protected settler communities\, and contributed to pivotal battles. D
 espite the hardships of disease\, displacement\, and warfare\, the Catawba
  demonstrated extraordinary resilience. Their story is one of courage\, al
 liance\, and survival\, woven into the struggle for independence in the So
 uthern Campaign of the Revolution.\n\nThe exhibit will run from June 30\, 
 2026 until October 24\, 2026. Admission is Free!
GEO:35.239004;-81.342181
LOCATION:Kings Mountain Historical Museum
SUMMARY:Choosing Sides: The Catawba Nation & The Fight for Independence
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/choosing-sides-the-catawba-n
 ation-the-fight-for-independence
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
