DESCRIPTION:The Python Crash Course: Introduction to Python introduces basi
 c concepts in the Python programming language such as object types\, base 
 Python data structures\, file paths\, and flow control (if statements & fo
 r-loops). We'll work through some applied examples and help you get Python
  installed on your computer.\n\n \n\nWe will also survey some of the popul
 ar packages for data science in Python and talk about next steps on your l
 earning journey.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is offered by University Library an
 d will be led by librarians Philip McDaniel\, Lorin Bruckner\, Michele Hay
 slett\, Matt Jansen\, and Rolando Rodriguez along with Mark Reed from ITS 
 Research Computing. Contact Matt Jansen with any questions.\n\n \n\nThis w
 orkshop is offered via Zoom. Register here: https://calendar.lib.unc.edu/e
 vent/17236560
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Python Crash Courses: Intro to Python
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/python-crash-courses-intro-to-
 python
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
