X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_b32e7018b18e1a8650f0d178e5d8314fd6664c368233eead570b44e368f882c9
SUMMARY:Public School Strong Organizing Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T203000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041810Z
UID:5abcc0mm4gsl10shb3om22nhsa@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261013T190000
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260122T230527Z
DESCRIPTION:Link to join: https://www.mobilize.us/join/46979990/1:84e2f965
 f1d120cd93fb7dd98f0d0b973c3029e538f77728a4e9c31ba0d1055d/\n\nHow to join:\
 nHi there\, \n\nThanks for signing up for our Public School Strong Orienta
 tion & Organizing Meeting!  \n\nBe sure to register on zoom in advance for
  this meeting:\nhttps://raceforward-org.zoom.us/meeting/register/tZIvcuiur
 z4pE9BGsfJi-mBBX_lhl2bPG7Ti \n\nAfter registering\, you will receive a con
 firmation email containing information about joining the meeting.\n\n**We 
 are thrilled to welcome David Backer\, author of As Public As Possible: Ra
 dical Finance for America’s Public Schools\, as our guest speaker at Jan
 uary’s meeting.** \n\nJoin us for the next Public Schools Strong organiz
 ing meeting on Thursday\, January 22nd\, where parents\, family members\, 
 educators\, and supporters from across the nation gather each month to gai
 n practical tools to promote\, protect\, and strengthen our public schools
 . \n\n*If you have already attended a Public School Strong Orientation\, y
 ou'll join a breakout room with current members for connection\, reflectio
 n and training. If you're new\, we've got you covered too!*\n\n**Do you wa
 nt honest\, equitable and fully-funded public schools?** Acting locally is
  key.\n\n### Join public school families\, educators and supporters from a
 cross the country to learn how to:\n1. Form a Public School Strong team in
  your school district\n2. Engage your community to get school boards and d
 istrict leaders to speak up for equitable and fully funded public schools\
 n3. Connect your local advocacy to others for state and national impact\n\
 nFor more info\, please visit publicschoolstrong.org\n\n### Current Public
  School Strong Members\n\nThere is strength in staying connected. After co
 mpleting Public School Strong (PSS) Orientation\, this is your consistent 
 space to reconnect with your peers across the country to:\n\n1. Access hel
 pful tools and practice relevant skills\,\n2. Connect the dots between wha
 t is happening locally and nationally\,\n3. Learn from mistakes and progre
 ss made along the way\n\nBring a friend!\n\n**Self Directed Orientation No
 w Available!**\n\nIf these live training times don't work for you\, you ca
 n complete your orientation at your own pace:\n\n1) Create Account in NEA 
 Portal (open to non-NEA members too): \n\nneapartnera.learnupon.com/users/
 sign_up\n\n2) Select the PSS orientation by clicking on this link:\n\nbit.
 ly/SelfDirectedPSS\n\nHow to prepare:\n### Hi there! Thanks for signing up
  for a 'Public School Strong Organizing Meeting!' (for new folks we'll als
 o have a new member orientation)\n\nThis event is virtual\, will provide u
 pdates on the federal attacks on our public schools and the immigrant comm
 unity\, actions you can take right now and the tools to support you in doi
 ng son. \n\nFor new folks\, we'll provide an introduction to our Public Sc
 hool Strong campaign. Check out our organizing platform using this link to
  find or create a local team: \n\n- publicschoolstrong.org\n\nMore on this
  powerful tool at your Orientation...\n\nhttps://www.mobilize.us/raceforwa
 rd/event/596321/
LAST-MODIFIED:20260122T230527Z
LOCATION:Virtual event
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (Virtual US)
END:VEVENT
