UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53682538096852
DTSTART:20261014T220000Z
DTEND:20261014T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:What happens in your brain when music moves you to tears? What 
 can we advance in neuroscience when a researcher asks why a melody can unl
 ock a memory\, ease anxiety\, or help a patient heal? \n\n \n\nFor years\,
  Renée Fleming has worked alongside physicians and researchers to better 
 understand the profound relationship between music and human health. In th
 is conversation\, presented in partnership with the UNC School of Medicine
  and moderated by arts and culture journalist Liza Roberts\, Fleming and U
 NC neuroscientists and practitioners explore how the arts are informing cu
 tting-edge developments and reshaping clinical practice.\n\n \n\nThe discu
 ssion moves beyond theory and into applications that touch everyday life: 
 how creative experiences matter to your well-being\, and how scientists ar
 e establishing important roles for the arts in healing\, connection\, and 
 human flourishing.\n\n \n\nThis is a rare opportunity to hear artists\, sc
 ientists\, and medical professionals share the same stage and to discover 
 how one of humanity’s oldest forms of expression is shaping the future o
 f health care.\n\n \n\nPlease note: Renée Fleming will not be performing 
 during this program. Join us for her separately-ticketed performance on Oc
 tober 13.\n\n \n\nStudent tickets always $11. Eligible for CLE. Find out m
 ore and buy tickets at: https://carolinaperformingarts.org/events/musicmin
 d/
GEO:35.911208;-79.051989
LOCATION:Memorial Hall
SUMMARY:Renée Fleming Music & Mind
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/renee-fleming-music-mind
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
