BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/john-lawson-legacy-days"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041837Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53796856316992
DTSTART:20261016T210000Z
DTEND:20261017T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:Step back in time and experience the history of eastern North C
 arolina during the 15th Annual John Lawson Legacy Days\, hosted by the Gri
 fton Historical Museum & Indian Village.\n\nThis multi-day living history 
 event brings the past to life through historical demonstrations\, reenacto
 rs\, guest speakers\, exhibits\, hands-on activities\, period crafts\, and
  educational programs exploring the people and events that shaped North Ca
 rolina. Visitors can learn about explorer and naturalist John Lawson\, Nat
 ive American history and culture\, colonial life\, early settlement\, and 
 the rich heritage of eastern North Carolina.\n\nThe 2026 celebration will 
 be especially meaningful as John Lawson Legacy Days coincides with the 50t
 h anniversary of the Grifton Historical Museum and the nationwide America2
 50 commemoration of the 250th anniversary of American independence.\n\nPro
 grams throughout the weekend will offer something for history lovers of al
 l ages\, from living history and demonstrations to special presentations a
 nd family-friendly activities. The weekend will also include opportunities
  to explore the museum and discover the fascinating history found right he
 re in eastern North Carolina.\n\nJoin us October 16–18\, 2026\, as we ce
 lebrate 15 years of John Lawson Legacy Days\, 50 years of preserving Grift
 on's history\, and 250 years of America's story.\n\nLocation: Grifton Hist
 orical Museum & Indian Village\, Grifton\, NC
GEO:35.368992;-77.432479
LOCATION:Grifton Historical Museum & Indian Village
SUMMARY:John Lawson Legacy Days
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/john-lawson-legacy-days
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/park-hangs-real-companion"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041837Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53817614037821
DTSTART:20261016T210000Z
DTEND:20261017T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Unwind and socialize at Park Hangs\, an outdoor concert series 
 at Bailey Park\n\nGather and unwind to the alt-country rock sounds of Real
  Companion from 6:00–8:00 pm. Food truck service begins at 5:00 pm.\n\nB
 ased in Boone\, Real Companion is an alt-country rock and folk-adjacent ou
 tfit fronted by Seth Sullivan. Their debut full-length album Nü-metal Her
 oes was recorded in a backyard studio\, drawing inspiration from a winding
  path towards sobriety\, parenthood\, and cheeseburgers.\n\n“Nü-metal H
 eroes feels off-the-cuff but fully developed—whether the duo are trying 
 their hand at spirited country-rockers or more streamlined\, almost dreamy
  folk-pop\, their instrumental contributions are pleasing but never taking
  away from the yarns Sullivan spins at the center of the songs. It all amo
 unts to a palpably Appalachian rock record—one that isn’t constrained 
 by its roots\, but that bears the marks of them nonetheless.”\n— Rosy 
 Overdrive\n\n \n\nPark Hangs\n\nJoin us to unwind and socialize at a new o
 utdoor concert series with music by NC-based artists\, food and drinks by 
 local vendors\, and easygoing vibes in Bailey Park (445 Patterson Ave. in 
 Winston-Salem). Park Hangs is presented by NCMA Winston-Salem and Innovati
 on Quarter\, with additional support from Atwell Ford Real Estate.\n\nBrin
 g your own food or purchase from vendors in the park or from favorite rest
 aurants in Innovation Quarter. Drinks from Incendiary Brewing will be avai
 lable for purchase\; outside alcohol is prohibited. Limited street parking
  is available\, with additional paid parking in the Link Parking Deck (530
  North Patterson Ave.).\n\nRSVP
GEO:36.099305;-80.24067
LOCATION:Bailey Park
SUMMARY:Park Hangs: Real Companion
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/park-hangs-real-companion
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
CATEGORIES:Concerts (Music)
END:VEVENT
