BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/spill-the-tea-7522"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041837Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52506845980223
DTSTART:20261018T190000Z
DTEND:20261018T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:​Spill the Tea! is a bold new musical inspired by the first r
 ecorded act of women's activism in American history — the Edenton Tea Pa
 rty. At the heart of the story is Penelope Barker\, the daring woman who o
 rganized 50 other women to sign a public resolution boycotting British goo
 ds — and sent it directly to King George III. This radical act of defian
 ce\, carried out in a time when women had no political voice\, helped spar
 k a revolution and laid the groundwork\, not only for the birth of a new n
 ation\, but for women to stand up for their rights.\n\nBlending pop\, hip-
 hop\, orchestral\, and classic Broadway musical styles\, Spill the Tea! is
  filled with humor\, heart\, and history. With a witty script plus lavish 
 sets and costumes\, the show celebrates the power of those who refused to 
 stay silent.​
GEO:36.299891;-76.219792
LOCATION:Arts of the Albemarle\, Maguire Theatre
SUMMARY:Spill the Tea!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/spill-the-tea-7522
CATEGORIES:Performances & Arts
CATEGORIES:Theater & Musicals
END:VEVENT
