BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/mapping-what-matters-a-workshop-on-logic-models-for-program-evaluation"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041913Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53204299869888
DTSTART:20261019T170000Z
DTEND:20261019T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Odum Institute in collaboration with Abacus Evaluation pres
 ents this 2‑hour online course that will include hands-on practice.\n\nT
 his course introduces participants to the use of logic models as practical
  tools for program evaluation.\n\nLogic models provide a structured way to
  articulate program theory\, clarify assumptions\, and make explicit the p
 athways through which program inputs and activities or strategies are expe
 cted to lead to outcomes and impact. In this course\, participants will le
 arn the core components and types of logic models\, examine real‑world e
 xamples\, and practice developing logic models for a program or project. T
 he course will also demonstrate how logic models can be used to guide deci
 sions about what to measure and when.\n\nThis course is designed for anyon
 e including researchers\, program staff\, and students who want a clear\, 
 systematic approach to evaluating programs and projects.\n\nRegistration a
 nd fee required to receive Zoom link access.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Mapping What Matters: A Workshop on Logic Models for Program Evalua
 tion
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/mapping-what-matters-a-worksho
 p-on-logic-models-for-program-evaluation
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
