BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/digital-accessibility-pop-up-labs"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041914Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53602941974007
DTSTART:20261109T160000Z
DTEND:20261109T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:The POP Lab is a drop-in workspace where UNC faculty and staff 
 can make progress with support from digital accessibility consultants. Bri
 ng your documents\, course materials\, websites\, reports\, or questions\,
  and work at your own pace. Come by for a few minutes or stay for the full
  session to ask questions\, explore tools\, solve problems and make meanin
 gful progress toward expanding access.\n\n \n\nProgress Over Perfection\n\
 nProgress means recognizing common barriers in the platforms you use and t
 aking small steps to reduce them. It’s choosing web formats over PDFs\, 
 applying table headers\, checking color contrast and collaborating on acce
 ssible templates so everyone can start from a strong foundation. Digital a
 ccessibility depends on steady\, intentional progress\, not perfection\, t
 o expand access for all.
LOCATION:Carolina Union\, 2502
SUMMARY:Digital Accessibility Pop-Up Labs
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/digital-accessibility-pop-up-l
 abs
CATEGORIES:Academic Calendar
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/genai-tools-and-resources-in-the-clinical-setting-3201"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041914Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53753537029339
DTSTART:20261109T160000Z
DTEND:20261109T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Curious about how to use generative AI (genAI) to inform your c
 linical research and practice?\n\n \n\nThis session will cover the basics 
 of using genAI chatbots and AI-assisted tools for clinical information ret
 rieval and literature reviews. We’ll discuss the pros and cons of using 
 AI tools for different steps of the research process\, prompting strategie
 s\, and using GenAI for evidence reviews. A review of clinical genAI tools
  will be included.\n\n \n\nThis workshop is offered by the UNC Health Scie
 nces Library and is led by Luke Barron\, Joel Collier\, and Beth Moreton. 
 It is part of the For Clinicians: Enhancing Practice Through Knowledge and
  Advancing Clinical Research Skills workshop tracks.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:GenAI Tools and Resources in the Clinical Setting
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/genai-tools-and-resources-in-t
 he-clinical-setting-3201
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_41d85e1478a55e3b4adbf2e4951c5be9f6e49241ac55a65427c71d252849bf1c
SUMMARY:Mobilization Mondays: Durham/Dacian Nation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261109T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261109T173000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041809Z
UID:dn2g099r7f03h5k5mu5ipkub80@google.com__20261109
SEQUENCE:2
CREATED:20260108T021652Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy and Dacian Nation 
 every Monday at Dacian Avenue and Washington Street in Durham from 4:30-5:
 30pm.  There is convenient parking.\n\nThis will be a POSITIVE and nonviol
 ent demonstration. We are here to protect our democracy. We are standing u
 p for what we believe in. We want to inspire people to join us and grow ou
 r movement!\n\nPlease bring positive signs supporting the movement and res
 isting what is happening in our country!\n\nPlease no mocking signs\, no s
 wastikas\n\nWe are excited to see you there and stand together for our cou
 ntry!\n\nSee you every Monday afternoon engaging drivers in Durham!\n\nPle
 ase join our Substack: <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://subst
 ack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy&amp\;sa=D&amp\;sou
 rce=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3y7Kv9RwiMPWcPPUFQih9k" target="_bl
