X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20260905T041838Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53601801757589
DTSTART:20261212T150000Z
DTEND:20261212T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Lake James State Park for “The History of Lake Jam
 es: From Native Lands to Modern Recreation.” This program explores the r
 ich cultural and historical timeline of the settlement and development of 
 Lake James\, from the Indigenous tribes who first lived along the banks of
  the rivers\, to the development of hydroelectric generation that created 
 the lake as we know it\, and finally to today’s recreational opportuniti
 es within the state park and surrounding area. It’s a great way to learn
  how the landscape and its uses have transformed over time while enjoying 
 the natural beauty of Lake James.
GEO:35.760718;-81.882276
LOCATION:Lake James State Park\, Visitor Center Classroom
SUMMARY:The History Lake James: From Native Lands to Modern Recreation
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/the-history-lake-james-from-
 native-lands-to-modern-recreation
