X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/madness-groove-folklore-fusion-for-flute-and-cello-wsn-26-27"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260905T041914Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53878949350255
DTSTART:20270401T233000Z
DTEND:20270402T004500Z
DESCRIPTION:FEATURING\n\nKelariz Keshavarz\, flute\nGrace Anderson\, cello\
 n\n \n\nPROGRAM\n\nJ.S. Bach / Gaspar Hoyos: Alemania Latina \nBach’s Pa
 rtita with Latin-groove bass line\n\nVilla-Lobos: The Jet Whistle\nBrazili
 an folk with counterpoint\n\nGaspar Cassadó: Intermezzo e Danza Finale fr
 om Solo Cello Suite\nAndalusian flamenco on the cello\n\nMarin Marais: Les
  Folies d’Espagne\nFrench baroque\, variations on an Iberian dance\n\nEv
 e Beglarian: I Will Not Be Sad in This World\nAn Armenian elegy for alto f
 lute and prerecorded audio\n\nReza Vali: Folk Songs set no. 9\nIranian fol
 k with extended techniques\n\n \n\nTICKETS\n\n$15 general admission\n$10 s
 tudents\, faculty\, and staff\nFree UNC Music students\, faculty\, and sta
 ff\n\nPurchase tickets online. Tickets are also available at the door\, 30
  minutes prior to the concert start time.\n\n \n\nPARKING\n\nPlease plan t
 o arrive early as parking on campus can be tricky. Learn more about parkin
 g and directions to UNC-Chapel Hill’s campus.\n\nThis event is part of t
 he 2026-2027 William S. Newman Artists Series\, a series of select concert
 s celebrating the alliance of scholarship and performance that animates th
 e lives of music faculty and students at Carolina.
GEO:35.912607;-79.053261
LOCATION:Hill Hall\, Moeser Auditorium
SUMMARY:Madness & Groove: Folklore Fusion for Flute and Cello | WSN 26-27
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/madness-groove-folklore-fusion
 -for-flute-and-cello-wsn-26-27
CATEGORIES:Performances
END:VEVENT
