DESCRIPTION:This exhibit explores how North Carolina helped forge a new nat
 ion during one of the most transformative periods in history. Through maps
 \, historical documents\, and everyday objects\, this exhibit reveals the 
 state’s role in the struggle for independence\, from early protests agai
 nst British rule and the battles fought on Carolina soil to the drafting o
 f the Constitution. Forging a Nation invites visitors to witness how ordin
 ary people\, conflict\, and conviction shaped North Carolina's history dur
 ing the American Revolution.
GEO:36.092774;-79.436435
LOCATION:May Memorial Library
SUMMARY:Forging A Nation: North Carolina in the America Revolution Exhibit
